The shacl-report binary, and the standalone HTML reports it writes, include the
third-party software listed below. Their license terms follow.

## Web viewer libraries

These JavaScript and CSS files are embedded in the binary, served by
`shacl-report serve` and inlined into standalone HTML reports.

| Library | Version | License | Files |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [Tabulator](https://tabulator.info) | 6.3.1 | MIT | `assets/vendor/tabulator/` |
| [MatGUI](https://github.com/Matdata-eu/MatGUI), Matdata's fork of [YASGUI](https://github.com/zazuko/Yasgui) | 6.6.0 | MIT | `assets/vendor/matgui/` |
| [CodeMirror 6](https://codemirror.net/) and [Lezer](https://lezer.codemirror.net/) | see `assets/vendor/codemirror/NOTICE.md` | MIT | `assets/vendor/codemirror/` |
| [codemirror-lang-turtle](https://github.com/aatauil/codemirror-lang-turtle) | 0.0.2 | MIT | `assets/vendor/codemirror/` |

The MatGUI bundle also contains the libraries below. Their license headers are
kept in the "Bundled license information" comment at the end of `matgui.min.js`.

